  "title": "Whina Cooper",
  "summary": "Dame Whina Cooper led a hikoi that set out from Te Hapua in Northland on 14 September 1975 and reached Parliament in Wellington on 13 October. About 5000 marchers arrived and a petition with 60,000 signatures went to Prime Minister Bill Rowling. The sources give no dated stops along the route.",
